{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateSelfDuality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateSelfDuality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Types.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.not_selfDualityMorphism_isIso_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.not_selfDualityMorphism_isIso_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L64-L78","doc":"**The former axiom `substrate_self_duality_axiom` was false** (removed\n2026-11-15, with its wrapper `substrate_self_duality`). It claimed that\n`selfDualityMorphism S` is an isomorphism for *every*\n`SelfDualPairingData`, but that structure carries no counit or snake\nlaws: `comul` and `frobeniusForm` are arbitrary morphisms. In `Type`, with\n`A = Bool` and `Δ b = (true, b)`, the morphism `φ` is constant at `true`,\nhence not injective. The true statement needs the Frobenius (snake)\nidentities as fields; recorded as open in bean `qou-n2un`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.selfDualityMorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.selfDualityMorphism","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L52-L62","doc":"The self-duality morphism `φ : A → A` induced by the Frobenius\npairing. Constructed as the composition:\n\n  A  →[Δ]  A ⊗ A  →[id ⊗ λ]  A ⊗ 𝟙  →[ρ]  A\n\nwhere Δ is comultiplication and λ is the Frobenius form.\nThis is the categorical analog of `a ↦ Σ a₍₁₎ · λ(a₍₂₎)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.comul","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Comultiplication `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.obj","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The underlying object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SelfDualPairingData","kind":"structure","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.lean#L23-L50","doc":"**Self-dual pairing data**: the object, comultiplication and\nFrobenius form that the self-duality morphism below consumes, and\nnothing else.\n\nThis is a file-local minimal carrier, **not** a Frobenius–Hopf\nsubstrate.  It was named `FrobeniusHopfSubstrate` until 2026-09-15,\nwhich collided — at the *fully qualified* name\n`QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate` — with the canonical\neight-field structure in `frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean` and with a\nthird three-field carrier in `categorical-reeb-derivation.lean`.\nNothing imported two of the three, so the collision was latent\nrather than a build error; renamed per bean `qou-hmhw`.\n\nWhat it is NOT, and the difference is load-bearing: it carries no\nmultiplication, no unit, no counit, no antipode and no laws — in\nparticular neither snake identity, so the non-degeneracy the\nself-duality claim below appeals to is *not* available from this\nstructure and is supplied as an external axiom.\n\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:substrate-self-duality","label":"thm:substrate-self-duality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-self-duality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}